      "severity": "major",
      "status": "open",
      "suggested_change": "Explicitly ask the learner to use vite, kjenne and kunne in the questions, or accept natural direct time questions without vite."
    },
    {
      "advisory": true,
      "block_hash": "fad48109f4d315980a2d99b393a225dfd7f90a3a697011cf5b6c0f9b7639e0e2",
      "citation_exact": true,
      "cited_excerpt": "States that the greenhouse closes at 18.00 as factual information, using a natural form of vite.",
      "created_against_sha256": "8c1315ffb5b1574c7c5e80f18a2d9a1a4355fcb5e7ddf0aa98a043feb63e1b9a",
      "criterion": "visible_prompt_rubric_alignment",
      "details": "Actual independent content review by /root/lesson_content_review_3; report SHA256 b803aef3454eeedee6da39d8ce850a131f827af633061a23b83e3d8800f95edf; original target revise_lea_message. Owner acceptance does not resolve this advisory.",
      "excerpt": "States that the greenhouse closes at 18.00 as factual information, using a natural form of vite.",
      "explanation": "The prompt asks for the closing time, personal acquaintance, learned task, and a comment about the week. It does not request the three knowing verbs. The schedule criterion nonetheless requires vite and the ability criterion requires kunne, rejecting a natural update such as «Drivhuset stenger klokka 18» or «Jeg lærte å justere vanningsanlegget».",
      "finding_id": "codex-knowing_verbs_vite_kjenne_kunne-3-1",
      "key": "revise_lea_message",
      "message": "",
      "previously_resolved": false,
      "quote_english": "",
      "resolution_comment": null,
      "resolution_note": "",
      "resolution_reason": null,
      "reviewer": "primary",
      "reviewer_version": "codex-independent-review-2026-10-25",
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "open",
      "suggested_change": "Add a visible instruction to express these facts using vite, kjenne and kunne, or stop making the exact verb choices binding."
    },
    {
